    "taxGuide.finland.source.vatRate": "Official tax source for the standard rate used by shared rule data. The ordinary traveller sale is for buyers not established in the EU or Norway, using habitual residence and permanent address evidence. The participating retailer or authorised refund business records passport, residence, detailed receipt, itemised goods, price and refund details, seals the package, and the unused goods and intact seal are inspected by Customs or the authorised desk. Export is in personal luggage within the official three-month period; final EU exit may be Finland or another member state, with Customs fallback if the authorised desk is unavailable. Permanent residents of Norway use a separate immediate-transport and Norwegian import-VAT proof route.",
    "taxGuide.sweden.eligibilitySummary": "Traveller eligibility. The traveller must live outside the EU, or meet the official move-from-Sweden rule and intend to live outside the EU for the required period. Goods are bought and carried by the traveller, unused, for non-commercial personal use, and covered by a participating retailer Tax Free receipt plus shop receipt, passport and travel documents. Swedish Customs currently says Sweden must be the last country visited before leaving the EU for this procedure. Tax Free partners handle partner documents and payment in Sweden; Swedish Customs handles fallback validation when the partner is closed, and validation is not payment.",
    "taxGuide.sweden.document.passport": "Passport or accepted identity document. The traveller must live outside the EU, or meet the official move-from-Sweden rule and intend to live outside the EU for the required period. Goods are bought and carried by the traveller, unused, for non-commercial personal use, and covered by a participating retailer Tax Free receipt plus shop receipt, passport and travel documents. Swedish Customs currently says Sweden must be the last country visited before leaving the EU for this procedure. Tax Free partners handle partner documents and payment in Sweden; Swedish Customs handles fallback validation when the partner is closed, and validation is not payment.",
