    "taxGuide.sweden.source.customsValidation": "Official authority source for validation, routing, baggage and fallback procedures. The traveller must live outside the EU, or meet the official move-from-Sweden rule and intend to live outside the EU for the required period. Goods are bought and carried by the traveller, unused, for non-commercial personal use, and covered by a participating retailer Tax Free receipt plus shop receipt, passport and travel documents. Swedish Customs currently says Sweden must be the last country visited before leaving the EU for this procedure. Tax Free partners handle partner documents and payment in Sweden; Swedish Customs handles fallback validation when the partner is closed, and validation is not payment.",
    "taxGuide.sweden.source.goodsConditions": "Official authority source for goods, luggage, unused-goods and exclusion conditions. The traveller must live outside the EU, or meet the official move-from-Sweden rule and intend to live outside the EU for the required period. Goods are bought and carried by the traveller, unused, for non-commercial personal use, and covered by a participating retailer Tax Free receipt plus shop receipt, passport and travel documents. Swedish Customs currently says Sweden must be the last country visited before leaving the EU for this procedure. Tax Free partners handle partner documents and payment in Sweden; Swedish Customs handles fallback validation when the partner is closed, and validation is not payment.",
    "taxGuide.sweden.source.vatRate": "Official tax source for the standard rate used by shared rule data. The traveller must live outside the EU, or meet the official move-from-Sweden rule and intend to live outside the EU for the required period. Goods are bought and carried by the traveller, unused, for non-commercial personal use, and covered by a participating retailer Tax Free receipt plus shop receipt, passport and travel documents. Swedish Customs currently says Sweden must be the last country visited before leaving the EU for this procedure. Tax Free partners handle partner documents and payment in Sweden; Swedish Customs handles fallback validation when the partner is closed, and validation is not payment.",
    "taxGuide.norway.eligibilitySummary": "Traveller eligibility. Norway is not an EU procedure. The traveller must be resident abroad and agree refund eligibility with the retailer because Norwegian Customs does not pay refunds. Official thresholds and proof routes depend on residence: residents of Sweden, Denmark and Finland use an import-VAT proof procedure, other residents use an invoice-based route, and Svalbard and Jan Mayen have separate treatment. Route one uses retailer form RD-0032 E, personal presentation of form and goods at a staffed customs location within one month after delivery, no retrospective attestation after departure, and retailer payment after the attested form is returned. Route two uses a private Tax-Free Shopping undertaking document that must not be stamped by Norwegian Customs; operator conditions and fees may apply.",
    "taxGuide.norway.document.passport": "Passport or accepted identity document. Norway is not an EU procedure. The traveller must be resident abroad and agree refund eligibility with the retailer because Norwegian Customs does not pay refunds. Official thresholds and proof routes depend on residence: residents of Sweden, Denmark and Finland use an import-VAT proof procedure, other residents use an invoice-based route, and Svalbard and Jan Mayen have separate treatment. Route one uses retailer form RD-0032 E, personal presentation of form and goods at a staffed customs location within one month after delivery, no retrospective attestation after departure, and retailer payment after the attested form is returned. Route two uses a private Tax-Free Shopping undertaking document that must not be stamped by Norwegian Customs; operator conditions and fees may apply.",
    "taxGuide.norway.document.residenceProof": "Reliable residence evidence. Norway is not an EU procedure. The traveller must be resident abroad and agree refund eligibility with the retailer because Norwegian Customs does not pay refunds. Official thresholds and proof routes depend on residence: residents of Sweden, Denmark and Finland use an import-VAT proof procedure, other residents use an invoice-based route, and Svalbard and Jan Mayen have separate treatment. Route one uses retailer form RD-0032 E, personal presentation of form and goods at a staffed customs location within one month after delivery, no retrospective attestation after departure, and retailer payment after the attested form is returned. Route two uses a private Tax-Free Shopping undertaking document that must not be stamped by Norwegian Customs; operator conditions and fees may apply.",
